stems comprising software and calibration services that reduce emissions and enhance fuel economy for traditional and hybrid applications. The Aftermarket segment engages in the provision of maintenance, test equipment, and vehicle diagnostics solutions; original equipment service solutions and remanufactured products; and sale of starters and alternators to original equipment manufacturers. Its products are used for commercial vehicles and industrial applications, such as medium-duty and heavy-duty trucks, buses and other off-highway construction, marine, agricultural and aerospace and defense applications; light commercial vehicles comprising vans and trucks; and light passenger vehicles, including passenger cars, mini-vans, cross-overs and sport-utility vehicles. PHINIA Inc. was incorporated in 2023 and is based in Auburn Hills, Michigan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brady D. Ericson | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $258K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 18\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["PHINIA Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.6B market cap on $3.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 22% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $188M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.40\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 60% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 38% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PHINIA (NYSE:PHIN) Climbs Past A Long-Term Line: What\u2019s Next?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/phinia-nysephin-climbs-past-a-long-term-line-whats-next","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794494040.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Is PHINIA (PHIN) Drawing Fresh Attention After Its Latest Update?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-phin/phinia/news/why-is-phinia-phin-drawing-fresh-attention-after-its-latest","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794493719.064,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Earnings Guidance Raised Might Change The Case For Investing In PHINIA Stock (PHIN)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-phin/phinia/news/earnings-guidance-raised-might-change-the-case-for-investing-1","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793982638.599,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (PHIN) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/Understanding_the_Setup:_PHIN_and_Scalable_Risk_110526120802_1793898482.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793898482.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"PHINIA (PHIN) Raises 2026 Outlook As Strong Results Put Valuation Back In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-phin/phinia/news/phinia-phin-raises-2026-outlook-as-strong-results-put-valuat","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793885344.735,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.91,"tier":0,"s